<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f4f1e9] text-slate-950">
  <header id="chatgpt-comparison-hero" class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <p class="border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
        ChatGPT alternative for research
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl">
        A ChatGPT alternative for research that needs structure.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
        A useful answer is a starting point. RationalGrid keeps each follow-up, challenge and
        source connected to the idea it concerns, so you can find it again and build on it with others.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          id="chatgpt-start-cta"
          href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
          data-analytics-event="comparison_start_grid_clicked"
          data-analytics-comparison="chatgpt"
          data-analytics-placement="hero"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-slate-800"
        >Start a grid <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
        <a
          id="chatgpt-ai-link"
          href="/intro/ai"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-500 px-1 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition hover:border-teal-700 hover:text-teal-800"
        >How RationalGrid uses AI <.icon name="hero-arrow-up-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <section id="chatgpt-verdict" aria-labelledby="chatgpt-verdict-heading">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">Short verdict</p>
      <h2
        id="chatgpt-verdict-heading"
        class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight"
      >
        Neither format wins every task.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Choose chat when speed and a flowing exchange matter most. Choose a grid when you expect to revisit a claim, follow several paths, attach evidence, or show someone else how the inquiry developed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="chatgpt-at-a-glance" class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="chatgpt-table-heading">
      <h2 id="chatgpt-table-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        At a glance
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto border border-stone-300 bg-white">
        <table
          id="chatgpt-comparison-table"
          class="w-full min-w-[44rem] border-collapse text-left"
        >
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-stone-100">
              <th class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">Need</th><th class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">
                ChatGPT
              </th><th class="bg-teal-950 px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white">
                RationalGrid
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-300 text-sm leading-6">
            <%= for {need, chat, grid} <- [
              {"Quick answer or draft", "Usually the more direct format.", "Possible, but more structure than the task may need."},
              {"Extended inquiry", "Keep related chats, files and instructions in a project.", "Keep connected branches in one navigable map."},
              {"Challenge a specific claim", "Quote it or ask a follow-up in the thread.", "Branch a challenge from the exact idea it addresses."},
              {"Evidence and sources", "Ask for sources and verify them.", "Keep evidence and source branches beside the relevant claim; verification still matters."},
              {"Find it again", "Search past chats or return to a project.", "Search My Learning, browse topics and collections, or return through a bookmark or highlight."},
              {"Build with others", "Collaborate through shared projects.", "Share a grid and add questions or challenges to specific ideas, keeping the exploration visible."}
            ] do %>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="bg-[#f8f6f0] px-5 py-4 font-semibold">{need}</th><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">
                  {chat}
                </td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-700">{grid}</td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="chatgpt-strengths"
      class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2"
      aria-label="What each option does well"
    >
      <article class="border-t-4 border-sky-600 bg-white p-6">
        <.icon name="hero-chat-bubble-left-right" class="h-6 w-6 text-sky-700" /><h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
          What ChatGPT does well
        </h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
          ChatGPT supports conversation, drafting, analysis and research. Search and shared
          projects help you return to work and collaborate across related chats and files.
          <a
            href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10169521-projects-in-chatgpt"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-teal-800 underline underline-offset-4"
          >See ChatGPT’s project features.</a>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border-t-4 border-teal-700 bg-slate-950 p-6 text-white">
        <.icon name="hero-share" class="h-6 w-6 text-teal-300" /><h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
          What RationalGrid does well
        </h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
          Explore several questions from one idea without losing their connections.
          Organise grids into topics, collections and folders in My Learning; bookmark a point
          or highlight a passage to revisit. Share the grid so others can examine the reasoning
          and take a branch further.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section
      id="chatgpt-choose"
      class="mt-14 border-y border-stone-300 py-10"
      aria-labelledby="chatgpt-choose-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="chatgpt-choose-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Which should you choose?
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-7 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Choose ChatGPT if…</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-slate-600">
            <li>• You want a fast response or working draft.</li><li>
              • A linear back-and-forth is easy to follow.
            </li><li>
              • You prefer keeping related chats and files in a project.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Choose RationalGrid if…</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-slate-600">
            <li>• Several questions or disagreements may grow from one starting point.</li><li>
              • Evidence, sources, notes, and challenges need to stay beside what they concern.
            </li><li>• You want to find saved ideas and build on them with others.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="chatgpt-caveat"
      class="mt-12 border border-stone-300 border-l-4 border-l-amber-600 bg-white p-6"
    >
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">A shared limitation</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Structure does not make an AI answer true. Both workflows require judgement: inspect sources, distinguish evidence from interpretation, and revise the question when its assumptions are weak.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="chatgpt-faq" class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="chatgpt-faq-heading">
      <h2 id="chatgpt-faq-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold">FAQ</h2><div class="mt-6 divide-y divide-stone-300 border-y border-stone-300">
        <%= for {question, answer} <- [
        {"Can ChatGPT handle complex research?", "It can support complex work, including analysis, files, and research-oriented tasks. The distinction here is the working format: RationalGrid keeps the branching relationships visible and durable."},
        {"Why not just use chat history or Projects?", "Those already help you keep and find work. RationalGrid adds a different way to explore it: each question, challenge and source stays attached to a specific idea, with bookmarks and highlights to return to that point."},
        {"Which is better for sources?", "Either can surface sources, and neither removes the need to inspect them. RationalGrid is designed to keep source and evidence branches attached to the claim they support."}
      ] do %>
          <details class="py-5">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">{question}</summary><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
              {answer}
            </p>
          </details>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav
      id="chatgpt-related-comparisons"
      class="mt-14 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8"
      aria-label="Related comparisons"
    >
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">Keep comparing</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold">
        <a
          href="/compare/kialo"
          class="text-teal-800 underline decoration-stone-400 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-teal-700"
        >Explore a free Kialo alternative</a>
        <a
          href="/compare/mind-maps"
          class="text-teal-800 underline decoration-stone-400 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-teal-700"
        >Argument maps vs mind maps</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <section id="chatgpt-final-cta" class="mt-14 bg-teal-950 p-7 text-white sm:p-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold">Give the next question somewhere to go.</h2><p class="mt-3 text-teal-100">
        Start with one question, then keep each answer, challenge, and source in context.
      </p><a
        id="chatgpt-final-cta-link"
        href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
        data-analytics-event="comparison_start_grid_clicked"
        data-analytics-comparison="chatgpt"
        data-analytics-placement="final_cta"
        class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-teal-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950 hover:bg-teal-200"
      >Start a free grid <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>
